# oracle: ELECTRODE piston in.piston cut to run 0 (dynamics, rigid wall and drag removed): pppm/electrode 1e-4 slab 3.0, fix electrode/conp algo cg 1e-4, symm on; atoms not compared (the wall forces of the cut-down fixes are not in the case)
# oracle-inputs: w68elec_piston.data
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): G vector 0.32814871, grid 12 15 36, order 5 (pppm/electrode 1e-4, slab 3.0); the engine chooses the same G and grid itself (no kspace_modify gewald/mesh); step 0: c_qwa=-0.0429634836159958 c_qau=0.0429634836159957 f_fxele=0 (the thermo row of the cut-down run)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.8e-14, atoms 0.
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): thermo max relative error 8.1e-12 (step 0); per-atom not compared
boundary        p p f
atom_style      full
units           real
kspace_style    pppm/electrode 1e-4
kspace_modify   slab 3.0
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long 8 8
bond_style      harmonic
angle_style     harmonic
read_data       w68elec_piston.data
pair_coeff 1 1 0.069 2.78
pair_coeff 2 2 5.29 2.951
pair_coeff 3 3 0.1553 3.166
pair_coeff 4 4 0.0 0.0
bond_coeff 1 600.0 1.0
angle_coeff 1 75.0 109.47
group wall type 1
group gold type 2
group spce type 3:4
group ele union wall gold
fix fRattleSPCE spce shake 0.0001 10 0 b 1 a 1
pair_modify mix arithmetic
neigh_modify every 1 delay 0
variable q atom q
compute qwa wall reduce sum v_q
compute qau gold reduce sum v_q
fix fxele ele electrode/conp 0.0 1.805 symm on algo cg 1e-4
thermo_style    custom step c_qwa c_qau f_fxele
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run 0
